    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "fca4f477fd2f7830e943418f9a94f009",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"interactive-audio-waveform-visualization\">\ud83c\udfb5 Interactive Audio Waveform Visualization</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This demo showcases a custom <code>anywidget</code> that integrates <strong>wavesurfer.js</strong> with marimo\nfor interactive audio waveform visualization and segment annotation.</span>\n<h2 id=\"features\">Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\ud83c\udfa8 <strong>Visual Waveform</strong>: See your audio as an interactive waveform</li>\n<li>\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f <strong>Draggable Regions</strong>: Mark segments with labels and colors</li>\n<li>\u23ef\ufe0f <strong>Playback Controls</strong>: Play/pause with live time tracking</li>\n<li>\ud83d\udd04 <strong>Two-Way Sync</strong>: Click table rows or waveform regions for bidirectional updates</li>\n<li>\ud83d\udccf <strong>Timeline</strong>: Time axis for precise positioning</li>\n</ul>\n<hr /></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bkHC",
      "code_hash": "5b557f3bfa25303c8e33bce1f4c53092",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"step-1-load-sample-audio\">Step 1: Load Sample Audio</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For this demo, you'll need to provide an audio file. You can:</span>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Upload an MP3/WAV file</strong> using the file picker below, OR</li>\n<li><strong>Use a sample file</strong> from your project (e.g., Torah reading audio)</li>\n</ol>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Supported formats: MP3, WAV, OGG, M4A</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Xref",
      "code_hash": "0e8bebfa538f0cbde462d48d9dea6a91",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"step-2-define-audio-regions\">Step 2: Define Audio Regions</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Regions represent segments of audio with start/end times and labels.\nThese could be:</span>\n<ul>\n<li>Verses in a Torah reading</li>\n<li>Chapters in a podcast</li>\n<li>Speakers in an interview</li>\n<li>Sections in a song</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Modify the regions below or let them auto-generate based on audio duration!</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Kclp",
      "code_hash": "b79ba783076acceaa9eb637b82f77bcd",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"step-4-regions-table-two-way-sync\">Step 4: Regions Table (Two-Way Sync)</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Click a row in the table to seek to that region in the waveform.\nDrag region boundaries in the waveform to update the table!</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
